From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] AUTO_MEMORIES_REGFILES: register files of placed standard
 cells, built by generate_ram
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A register file, many ports over few words, is not an SRAM: FakeRAM's
single-port model does not describe it, and synthesised to flops its
mux trees are placed by a placer that does not know they are an array.

AUTO_MEMORIES_REGFILES lists spec files, one per RTL module.
memories/regfile_ram.py translates each to OpenROAD generate_ram_netlist
options (ports, banks, folds, the zero word, reset, read latency, write
style and priority, cells), checks it against the module's ports from
synthesis (a stray, missing or mis-sized port stops the build), and
writes a wrapper in the module's place around the RAM, <m>_ram: an
active-high reset inverted for an active-low flop, addresses narrowed
or widened. A register file is inlined unless AUTO_MEMORIES_MACRO_PLACE
names it: its cells are then placed, sized and buffered with the rest
of the design. A named one is a macro to synthesis and macro placement
(an abstract LEF and a liberty of its area beside the FakeRAM views, in
blackboxes.txt; a parameterized module's instances lose parameters the
netlist does not declare). In `mode netlist` it dissolves into its
cells at the end of macro placement (regfile_dissolve.tcl): the core
FIRM where the placer put the macro, flipped as it was, row parity
kept; the periphery left to global placement and the resizer; then
eliminate_dead_logic. `mode macro` keeps it, with pins, a power grid
and a timing model from write_timing_model.

Where a row holds several words they sit side by side, and a word whose
bits would run more than 150 um is folded into more rows: XiangShan's
RobEntryFile and RenameBufferFile, dissolved into a parent, did not
legalize otherwise (the parent buffers the word's selects inside the
full array).

A module named in a spec whose memory has an initial value stops the
build: generate_ram's storage has none, and the value would be lost
without a word. The spec's read_latency, a key shared with
structured_gen's specs, is generate_ram's -register_read_address.

The RAMs the wrappers instantiate as macros are listed in
regfile_cores.txt: they are in blackboxes.txt but no module of the
sources, so ORFS's check that every AUTO_MEMORIES module is a black box
after read_slang skips them.

Needs generate_ram's register-file options, OpenROAD #11723 (merged).
Not upstreamed;
retires at a //:bump onto an ORFS that carries it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
